NUM-09: update a surcharged node with no head-dependent links from its surface area

initGeometry() reproduces the legacy crown of an outlet (yFull = TINY), so a
junction drained only by outlets is EXTRAN-surcharged at any depth, and the
explicit branch of DWSolver::setNodeDepth() computes dy = dQ / sumdqdh = 0:
the depth freezes and the inflow is lost. Use the surface-area update for
any node with sumdqdh = 0, not only storage units, as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-09_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/DynamicWave.cpp
